      "message": "I skimmed through every usage of DAWN_UNREACHABLE and I think this will be OK.\nI was looking for cases where it looked like we meant \"crash in debug but ignore in release\". (I *did* find some cases where there\u0027s code after a DAWN_UNREACHABLE, at least some of these were incorrectly treating it as a \"crash in debug, noop in release\".) I also tried to use Gemini to slightly more smartly look for weird cases but didn\u0027t find anything else.\n\nIf this sticks, we should change all DAWN_CHECK(false) to DAWN_UNREACHABLE.",
